00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,580
(Not even close)

280
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,800
Hu, come try.

281
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,520
See if you can reach.

282
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:47,380
(Human prop reporting for duty)

283
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,300
(One effortless lift)

284
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:01,320
What the heck was that?

285
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,680
That works.

286
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,280
He lifted you like a picture frame

287
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,400
and hung you right up.

288
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,240
Losing this 1 kg really paid off.

289
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,560
I was like a little chick.

290
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:11,840
He just stuck me right up there.

291
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,040
Good thing it wasn't Chengcheng.

292
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,400
He would've lifted him too high.

293
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,360
My neck would've cleared it.

294
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,240
Don't do that to him.

295
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,600
That has to hurt.

296
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,400
I'm telling you.

297
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,880
Let me try it with the hat.

298
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:26,760
Hu.

299
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:29,160
(Human prop back in action)

300
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:29,840
Lean back.

301
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,440
Lean back. Don't touch it.

302
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,520
Don't touch.

303
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,220
(Only elbows can steady the hat)

304
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:37,860
(Every last ball is gone)

305
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,080
What's all this stuff on the ground?

306
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,520
Did you drop your brain cells?

307
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,000
Who shook them out?

308
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,720
(I've got a plan)
I'll grab him from behind.

309
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,680
You grab his legs.

310
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:50,840
We'll carry him over

311
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,520
to the door.

312
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,280
Then everyone helps him sit up.

313
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,840
One lift, and he's up there.

314
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,360
Okay.

315
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:57,780
(Okay?)

316
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,320
Okay?

317
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,080
Okay.

318
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,400
I'll grab his neck.

319
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,000
Just hold it like this.

320
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,480
Will I even make it there alive?

321
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,600
I'm starting to wonder.

322
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,800
How about this, Teng?

323
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,840
He'll support your neck from the front.

324
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,760
I'll hold it from behind.

325
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:10,880
If your head leans too far forward,

326
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,430
(Chengcheng's got his back)
I'll just yank it back.

327
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,880
Don't yank so hard that Teng

328
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,360
wakes up missing a chunk of his neck.

329
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:17,760
You can support his chin, right?

330
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,080
Or how about this?

331
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:19,840
I'll hold his chin

332
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,920
and pull it back like this.

333
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:21,720
Like this.

334
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,160
Just don't pull too hard.

335
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,120
His head will tip backward.

336
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,400
I won't.

337
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:29,880
Weren't you

338
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,040
the one laughing the hardest earlier?

339
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,520
Churan, could you move back

340
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:35,240
a little?

341
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,360
No way.

342
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,040
I swear,

343
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,240
I'm definitely innocent this round.

344
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:39,960
Every time you say that...

345
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:41,480
You're the bad guy.

346
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,200
(Zero credibility left)
You say it without even thinking.

347
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,040
I'm definitely innocent.

348
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:46,360
Actually, I even think

349
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,320
Bing and Chengcheng are the Impostors.

350
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,840
Should we start voting now?

351
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:54,040
(Guessing with zero clues)

352
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:55,880
Don't even need to play.

353
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:56,920
Let's give it a try. Come on.

354
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:59,000
(Automatic Door Troublemaker: Round 1)

355
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,080
Teng, lie back on my hand.

356
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,480
Rest your neck on my hand.

357
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,260
(Head support)

358
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,560
You're pushing me forward.

359
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:06,020
(The human prop can't move on his own)
How am I supposed to lie on your hand?

360
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:09,560
Lie back now.

361
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,720
Just like that.

362
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,440
Come on.

363
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:14,320
I'll get his hand.

364
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:16,960
Bing, put Teng's arm

365
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:17,720
over your shoulder.

366
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:20,360
Three, two, one, lift.

367
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,840
(Holding his entire waist)
Three, two, one, lift.

368
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,900
(Wang Churan: Chin.
Huang Jingyu: Right leg)

369
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,840
(Li: Right arm. Hu: Back of neck)
Okay, let's go!

370
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:29,160
(Bai: Lower back. Chengcheng: Left arm)
Slow down. No rush.

371
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,570
(Bing: Left leg)
Take it slow.

372
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,400
Easy does it.

373
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,720
Watch where you're going.

374
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,780
(Human prop has gone limp)

375
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:38,460
(Secretly watching his teammate)

376
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,700
(Too far away)

377
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,980
(Better give up for now)

378
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,740
(Pinch)

379
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:46,740
(Who's pinching me?)

380
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:49,180
(Giving it his all)

381
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:50,760
Come on, turn.

382
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,080
It's like we're on a farm,

383
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,320
carrying a scarecrow.

384
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,360
Come on, lift his upper body.

385
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:04,960
Come on!

386
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,040
One, two, three.

387
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,920
Lift!

388
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:11,360
Three.

389
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,040
Lift!

390
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,300
(10 cm)

391
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:15,680
Go!

392
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:27,460
(Almost lined up)

393
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:28,700
(Will they make it?)

394
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,500
(Pinch)

395
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,040
His head! His face!

396
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,260
(Hat brim in danger)

397
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,960
(Can't reach it)
No! The hat.

398
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,520
It's falling.

399
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,080
The hat.

400
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,800
No!

401
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:41,400
It's falling.

402
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,360
The hat.

403
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:43,560
(Instinctively trying to save it)
The hat.

404
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,160
No!

405
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:46,760
The hat.

406
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:47,280
It's falling.

407
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,960
The straw hat came off.

408
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,680
Mission failed.

409
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,660
(Hat came off. Mission failed)

410
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:56,180
(Thanks for the accidental assist)

411
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:57,720
No, it fell.

412
00:13:58,920 --> 00:13:59,920
Well, we definitely failed.

413
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,600
It fell.

414
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:02,640
It was falling, so I caught it.

415
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:03,920
You took it off?

416
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,640
It had already fallen.

417
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,830
(Well, this isn't good)
Oh, great. Now I'm the bad guy.

418
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,640
Come on, let's discuss.

419
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,920
Now I'm the bad guy.

420
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:14,960
You wanna leave on your own,

421
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,760
or should we vote you out?

422
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:17,480
Listen, Teng.

423
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:19,000
(Let me explain)
Here's why I grabbed the hat.

424
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,280
When you reached the door,

425
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,640
the hat was already like this.

426
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,520
Yeah, that's true.

427
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,560
It was already slipping sideways.

428
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,040
The door was pushing against my brim.

429
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,400
It really was sliding backward.

430
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,120
But still,

431
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:28,880
you shouldn't have

432
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:29,680
taken it off.

433
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,960
Not one ball had fallen.

434
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:32,880
I couldn't reach it.

435
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,640
You could've jumped up.

436
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,440
Jump and hit it with your elbow?

437
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,520
Who'd risk doing
something that dangerous?

438
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,760
My elbows are pretty strong.

439
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,240
I mean,

440
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:41,920
what if I hurt you?

441
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:43,880
(Was he really that worried about me?)

442
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:44,840
Vote him out first. We don't need him.

443
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:46,700
(Mr. Huang goes on the offensive)

444
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,120
You messed up the job,

445
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,280
and all you've got are excuses.

446
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:51,820
(Thanks, Mr. Huang. Right on cue)

447
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,600
But I'm really innocent.

448
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,680
An innocent player like you is useless.

449
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,120
(Useful to us Impostors, though)

450
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,560
Keeping you would only ruin

451
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,160
rounds two and three.

452
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:02,720
No.

453
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,960
(Someone prove my innocence)

454
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,720
I think he should be eliminated

455
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:07,440
before either of the two Impostors.

456
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:09,520
It's not that

457
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,200
I think he's an Impostor.

458
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,840
He's just too good at ruining things.

459
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:13,620
(We can't take any more)

460
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,000
My last words are

461
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,400
keep an eye on Li Yunrui.

462
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:20,280
Something's off about him.

463
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,000
(One suspect named)
Earlier,

464
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,960
(Suspects Li Yunrui is an Impostor)
while we were going around,

465
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:23,600
he kept

466
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,400
glancing at the hat.

467
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:27,040
I don't know if he wanted it to fall

468
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:27,960
or what.

469
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,480
Anyway...

470
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:29,320
I'm not so sure.

471
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,560
When you were carrying me,

472
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,560
Chengcheng

473
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,640
(Suspects Chengcheng is an Impostor)
was pinching me.

474
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:36,800
What?

475
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:40,460
(Another twist?)

476
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:41,800
When I first went limp,

477
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,240
my eyes were closed.

478
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:43,680
Then,

479
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:44,840
you started pinching me.

480
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,400
You pinched my arm.

481
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,240
No, Teng.

482
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,080
(Let me make an excuse)
You weigh a ton.

483
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,560
I'm not even kidding.

484
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,280
A ton.

485
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,520
Isn't this how you carry someone?

486
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:54,560
Nobody carries someone like that.

487
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:57,720
There's too much stuff
under your armpit.

488
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,240
I couldn't get a grip.

489
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,840
My lymph nodes got in your way,

490
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:01,400
huh?

491
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,520
No, that's just how I am.

492
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,600
I just pinched you a couple times.

493
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:08,920
Yeah.

494
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,720
At least you know your true nature.

495
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,720
Your stage name should be Fan Evil.

496
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,840
Lin's suspicious too.

497
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,430
(Back to Lin)
Yeah, Lin really

498
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,640
(Back on him again)
hasn't said a word.

499
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:24,880
No, seriously.

500
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:25,880
I couldn't really do much back there.

501
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:26,480
You know, I...

502
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,480
Weren't you right next to me?

503
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,280
Yeah, I saw you

504
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,400
take the hat off yourself.

505
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:33,720
I was stunned.

506
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:36,620
(Nice work)

507
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,960
I'm speechless.

508
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,520
His chest was high enough.

509
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:40,840
But the hat got caught...

510
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,220
On the action camera.

511
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,240
I've got it.

512
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,480
Tailbone.

513
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,640
That won't affect the hat. Really.

514
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,040
You barely managed with your chest,

515
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,600
(That's actually a good spot)
and now you want the tailbone?

516
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,240
What about the nose?

517
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,200
(I've got another idea)
What if we use the nose?

518
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,680
The nose would line up perfectly.

519
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,120
Just lift him a little.

520
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:58,080
Stop giving the Impostors ideas.

521
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,640
Oh my God.

522
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,360
The Impostors heard everything.

523
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,240
That's even better.

524
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,310
I've explained it so clearly.

525
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:05,240
Whoever doesn't follow the plan

526
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:06,240
must be an Impostor.

527
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,720
The Impostors choose
the person and body part,

528
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:10,480
not you.

529
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,590
How do you know so much?

530
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,720
I've already given a whole lecture.

531
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,310
What's the point of stopping me now?

532
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:22,440
I've explained everything in detail.

533
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:23,440
I've already handed in my paper.

534
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,830
You warned me way too late.

535
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,800
Everyone can vote now.

536
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,920
Three, two, one. Vote.

537
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,500
(Wang Churan: 1, Hu Xianxu: 5,
Fan Chengcheng: 1, Li Yunrui: 1)

538
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,340
(Hu Xianxu: 5 votes, out)

539
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,080
Did you vote me out, Teng?

540
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,480
I only had one vote.
I just pointed at you.

541
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,160
I'm switching places later.

542
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,280
(Getting away from the drama)

543
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:44,360
Hu is eliminated.

544
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:45,480
Hu

545
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:45,880
was innocent.

546
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,520
An innocent player is out.

547
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,760
So both Impostors are still here?

548
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:52,080
Yep.

549
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:54,640
You really thought it
was me, didn't you?

550
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,960
Why else would I vote for you?

551
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,240
Okay.

552
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,320
Everyone, close your eyes.

553
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,460
(Automatic Door Troublemaker: Round 2)

554
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,120
(Let me see)

555
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:08,080
Impostors, open your eyes.

556
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:10,560
(I knew it was you)

557
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,240
Impostors, please choose

558
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:15,040
(I knew it was you two)
the human prop and body part for this round.

559
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:15,920
When you point at someone,

560
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,000
lift your arm first.

561
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:17,800
(Still helping the Impostors)
Then do this.

562
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,760
So your clothes don't rustle.

563
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:21,900
(Huang Jingyu)

564
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:26,740
(Human prop: Huang Jingyu)

565
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,760
Which body part?

566
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:37,880
Three, two, one. Open your eyes.

567
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:39,960
Who'd they pick?

568
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,640
This round,

569
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,040
it's Jingyu's

570
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:45,000
toes.

571
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,540
(Human prop: Huang Jingyu.
Chosen body part: Toes)

572
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,680
How much do you weigh, Jingyu?

573
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,880
Under 90 kilos, I think.

574
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:53,140
(How are we supposed to lift him?)

575
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,400
His toes?

576
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,560
How do we keep the hat on?

577
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,480
Just pull the hat down tight.

578
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,080
I've got it.

579
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:01,800
The two tallest people here...

580
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:03,200
(Accidentally picked an Impostor)

581
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,400
We'll take Jingyu's legs

582
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,680
and put his feet on our shoulders.

583
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,040
Can we even carry him?

584
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,280
Someone else help me!

585
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,400
(Then let the other Impostor carry him)
I'll carry him.

586
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,000
I can do it.

587
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:16,560
Me too.

588
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,240
Are you trying to get me killed?

589
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:20,680
I can do it.

590
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:21,960
But we need to turn him sideways.

591
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:22,440
Sideways.

592
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:22,880
Otherwise,

593
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:23,920
if we hold him straight,

594
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:24,600
his heel will touch it.

595
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,800
We can bend his toes.

596
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:27,360
Bend his toes?

597
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,640
Or just chop them off.

598
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,280
Why not cut them off

599
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,360
and stick them on the circle?

600
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,920
(You've always got the best ideas)

601
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:34,440
I'll hold him.

602
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,400
I'll grab him from behind.

603
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:36,960
Yeah.

604
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,720
You're gonna hold me horizontally?

605
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,120
Yeah, horizontally.

606
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:41,040
Like...

607
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,240
Don't worry about the front.

608
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:48,080
Then I'll stand beside you
playing a trumpet.

609
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,360
Leave that job to the eliminated guy.

610
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,080
Let's go.

611
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:00,440
Let's have Lin and Churan

612
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:02,680
carry his legs.

613
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:03,800
No problem.

614
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:04,120
Okay.

615
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:04,520
What?

616
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,320
You've been talking big this whole time,

617
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,640
but what are you gonna do?

618
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:09,040
Churan said she could carry him.

619
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,280
I'll be in charge

620
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:10,840
of bending his toes.

621
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,080
I'm starting to think he's an Impostor.

622
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,160
Seriously.

623
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:16,440
(Taking the chance to pile on)

624
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,840
This round, I'll be Jingyu's

625
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:18,560
posture coach.

626
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,080
And we need someone

627
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,480
with a delicate touch

628
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,480
to pull his hat

629
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,160
down over his face.

630
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:27,720
That's crucial.

631
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:28,560
Don't tell me that's you.

632
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:30,860
(I'm afraid so)

633
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,040
Nobody else

634
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:34,080
has the patience or attention to detail.

635
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,880
(Too talented to stay humble)

636
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,200
Or the skills.

637
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,120
(It's all yours, then)

638
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,760
There are nine balls in here.

639
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:45,960
Ten, Teng.

640
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:46,360
Ten.

641
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:46,880
Ten?

642
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:47,520
Ten.

643
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:50,400
Mr. Huang, you're really...

644
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:51,780
(Honest to a fault)

645
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:52,840
Mr. Huang's an Impostor.

646
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:55,880
After all that scheming...

647
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:56,440
He counted

648
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,400
all ten.

649
00:20:58,640 --> 00:20:59,520
Mr. Huang.

650
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,520
(You ruined my plan)

651
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,720
You little punk.

652
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:02,920
We don't trust you anymore.

653
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,560
Stay over here with me.

654
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:05,240
Come on.

655
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:10,040
You're lifting my legs?

656
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:11,900
Easy, Churan.

657
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:12,920
If Churan lifts like that,

658
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,280
we can definitely get him up.

659
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:14,840
Come on.

660
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:15,640
He hasn't leaned back.

661
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:16,120
One, two, three.

662
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:16,880
Wrong leg.

663
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:19,265
(Churan: Right leg. Chengcheng: Right arm)
Easy.

664
00:21:19,265 --> 00:21:19,640
(Li: Left leg)
Easy.

665
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,160
Lean back.

666
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,600
(Taking most of the weight)

667
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,080
Come on.

668
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:26,720
Onto your shoulder.

669
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,240
Sound the horn.

670
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,280
Hold on.

671
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:30,580
(Official hat protector)

672
00:21:30,780 --> 00:21:31,910
(Wang Churan: Right leg. Fan Chengcheng:
Right arm. Li Yunrui: Left leg)

673
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:32,880
(Shen Teng: Hat. Jia Bing:
Head. Hu Xianxu: Band)

674
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:34,480
Let's get started already.

675
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,360
Let's move.

676
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:36,600
Start.

677
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:44,870
(Spoke too soon)
Come on. Left, right, left.

678
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,120
Left, right, left.

679
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:49,100
(Keeping the hat and head steady)

680
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:56,180
(Picking up the pace)

681
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:57,720
Who's going so fast?

682
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:00,300
(Getting dragged along)

683
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,420
(Hat tilting)

684
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,720
Who's rushing? Hold on.

685
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:11,280
You guys.

686
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:12,680
Where's Bai?

687
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,080
Bai.

688
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,800
I can hear him, but I can't see him.

689
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:16,680
I'm here!

690
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:21,720
Who's going so fast? Wait.

691
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:24,000
Bai's doing most of the lifting.

692
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:30,060
(So heavy)

693
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,160
I can't do this!

694
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,400
Can we go faster?

695
00:22:34,420 --> 00:22:36,900
(Weighs a ton)

696
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,800
Wang Churan,

697
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,400
why would you

698
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:42,880
take on something

699
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:44,480
you clearly can't handle?

700
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:48,780
(Such a thoughtful Impostor)

701
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:53,620
(Leaning forward)

702
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:56,220
(Getting things under control)

703
00:22:57,260 --> 00:22:59,340
(Pulling hard to the right)

704
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:08,340
(Steady in one move)

705
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:14,340
(Three balls lost)

706
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:15,600
Go!

707
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,020
(They still haven't failed?)

708
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:19,200
Hang in there.

709
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:19,640
Wait.

710
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:21,520
Come on.

711
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:28,660
(Switching positions on the fly)

712
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:33,920
Keep going.

713
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:34,880
Almost there.

714
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,320
Teng, point your toes.

715
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,460
(Mission accomplished)

716
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:40,880
Yes.

717
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:43,120
Nice.

718
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:46,840
Good. Seven balls left.

719
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:48,000
Congratulations.

720
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,640
(Challenge completed)
The innocent team wins this round.

721
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:50,400
No one gets eliminated.

722
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:57,240
Nice.

723
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:01,160
Great work.

724
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,280
Even I'm exhausted from that.

725
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,200
You were tightening your core too.

726
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:05,840
I could tell.

727
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:07,720
I don't think the three
at the back are Impostors.

728
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:11,360
(The three at the back)
If any of them had tried sabotaging us,

729
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:11,920
we would've failed.

730
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:12,200
Right.

731
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:14,280
At the worst moment,

732
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:16,320
Bing even reached in to help.

733
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,000
Scared me to death.

734
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:17,560
A hand came out of nowhere.

735
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:18,880
Yeah.

736
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:20,040
Exactly.

737
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:20,880
He really saved us.

738
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:21,280
Bing,

739
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:22,840
you're cleared.

740
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:23,280
Good.

741
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:25,080
(No longer a suspect)

742
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:26,040
Being innocent is exhausting.

743
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,000
Your leather jacket's soaked, huh?

744
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:28,480
You bet.

745
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:32,400
I think Lin's innocent too.

746
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:34,160
Why?

747
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,520
You all saw what happened.

748
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:37,720
The three at the back are innocent.

749
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:39,280
And you two up front are innocent too.

750
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:40,200
(Front two: Li Yunrui and Wang Churan)

751
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:41,130
(Human prop: Huang Jingyu.
What about me? Fan Chengcheng)

752
00:24:41,130 --> 00:24:42,010
(Back three: Bai Jingting,
Shen Teng and Jia Bing)

753
00:24:42,010 --> 00:24:42,580
(Eliminated: Hu Xianxu)

754
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:45,200
What were you doing back there?

755
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:48,280
I haven't said a word since.

756
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,080
I'm still catching my breath.

757
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:51,200
I'm exhausted, Jingyu.

758
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:52,080
Where were you?

759
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,800
I was holding your right arm.

760
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:56,900
(Fair enough)

761
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:58,920
I think the two at the front...

762
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:02,960
They suddenly sped up at one point.

763
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,760
When we turned here,

764
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:07,000
I was walking pretty...

765
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,480
They just dragged me along.

766
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,400
That's when the hat suddenly jerked.

767
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:10,720
Yeah.

768
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:12,760
How were you walking?

769
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:14,800
Were you facing backward?

770
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,000
I was like this.

771
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:18,560
Bai,

772
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:19,880
you really worked hard.

773
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,160
(The matching-color duo
understands each other)

774
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:22,280
He just wanted to show you

775
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:23,280
he's been training his legs.

776
00:25:28,880 --> 00:25:31,000
But we really did speed up at one point.

777
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,880
That might've been me.

778
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:33,920
First of all,

779
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:35,320
he was really heavy.

780
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:36,200
And second,

781
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,240
I was on the outside of the turn,

782
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:38,400
so I had

783
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,680
(Makes sense)
to take more steps than you guys.

784
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,560
Then who is it?

785
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:44,560
It's not us two.

786
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:46,240
Not him either.

787
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:48,320
So it's two out of five.

788
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:53,540
(What a breakthrough. Two out of five)

789
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:54,440
Alright, everyone.

790
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:56,960
Three, two, one. Close your eyes.

791
00:25:57,100 --> 00:25:58,360
(Automatic Door Troublemaker:
Round 3, the final showdown)

792
00:25:58,360 --> 00:26:00,120
Impostors, open your eyes.

793
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:04,400
Impostors, choose someone.

794
00:26:07,260 --> 00:26:09,340
(Human prop: Huang Jingyu)

795
00:26:09,380 --> 00:26:10,320
(Sensing another heavy lift coming)

796
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,360
Impostors, choose the body part.

797
00:26:16,780 --> 00:26:18,220
(Hip)

798
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:19,480
Okay, open your eyes.

799
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:21,400
This round's human prop

800
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:22,400
is Jingyu.

801
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,280
Body part, hip.

802
00:26:29,280 --> 00:26:30,740
(Human prop: Huang Jingyu.
Chosen body part: Hip)

803
00:26:31,880 --> 00:26:32,720
Are they trying to kill us?

804
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,040
He must've picked himself.

805
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:35,640
I swear I didn't.

806
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:36,880
His hip?

807
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:39,320
Two people could just carry him,

808
00:26:39,320 --> 00:26:39,800
right?

809
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,880
No, we'd have to lift him like this.

810
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,700
(Using the same plan as last round)

811
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:45,280
Then lift him upward.

812
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:46,800
Four people can carry him.

813
00:26:46,800 --> 00:26:47,280
That won't work because...

814
00:26:47,280 --> 00:26:47,640
No.

815
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:48,400
At the end,

816
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:49,920
you won't get his hip against it.

817
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:52,900
(Wait, what? Huh? Really?)

818
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,360
Actually, you could...

819
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:56,920
I could carry him on my back

820
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:57,840
while you lift him from behind.

821
00:26:57,860 --> 00:26:58,900
(This Impostor insists on a key position)

822
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,600
And then...

823
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:00,840
I'll straighten up.

824
00:27:00,840 --> 00:27:03,040
His hip would be way too high.

825
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:03,680
We couldn't lift him.

826
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:05,260
(Only halfway up)

827
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:06,920
You'd have to...

828
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:10,700
(No one will understand
this in a decade)

829
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,140
(Gymnastics training)

830
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:16,440
Gymnastics.

831
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,600
Team gymnastics.

832
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:20,720
No.

833
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,280
He has to stay completely limp.

834
00:27:22,310 --> 00:27:23,560
(The human prop can't move on his own)
He can't lift himself.

835
00:27:23,560 --> 00:27:24,280
Stand up straight.

836
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:25,840
If you don't squat,
he won't hang like that.

837
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:27,640
Let's try it first.

838
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,480
I'll take his legs.

839
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:29,960
Put them on my shoulders.

840
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:31,280
Bai.

841
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:32,720
Bai, the...

842
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:33,640
The front will be too high.

843
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:34,880
It's fine. I'll lower myself.

844
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,000
I'll bend over.

845
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:38,600
Come on.

846
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:39,370
(Bai Jingting: Both legs.
Jia Bing: Left arm)

847
00:27:39,380 --> 00:27:40,180
(Fan Chengcheng and Wang Churan:
Hat. Li Yunrui: Right arm)

848
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:42,940
(Checking things out first)

849
00:27:42,960 --> 00:27:43,320
Go.

850
00:27:43,580 --> 00:27:44,200
(Test run begins)

851
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,040
A donkey turns the millstone.

852
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:49,400
It keeps going around in circles.

853
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:50,720
Welcome to my hometown,

854
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:51,760
beautiful Huairou.

855
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:55,660
(Welcome to Beijing)

856
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,750
(Struggling)
Northernmost Beijing,

857
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,520
beautiful Huairou.

858
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:01,840
Come visit Huairou.

859
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:06,720
That's how welcoming
we Huairou folks are.

860
00:28:09,660 --> 00:28:12,340
(Warm, welcoming and dependable)

861
00:28:13,340 --> 00:28:14,960
(Aren't we just torturing ourselves?)
I can't do this.

862
00:28:15,780 --> 00:28:17,060
(This plan is too exhausting. Aborted)

863
00:28:18,660 --> 00:28:20,320
(Back to square one)

864
00:28:20,320 --> 00:28:21,760
What if someone rides
on my back to hold him?

865
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,640
Ride on you to hold him?

866
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:26,360
Yeah, someone sit on top
of me and hold him.

867
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,600
Sit on my shoulders.

868
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:30,000
No way.

869
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:30,760
And support him from behind.

870
00:28:30,760 --> 00:28:31,560
(Bai picks him again)

871
00:28:31,560 --> 00:28:32,480
That's impossible, isn't it?

872
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:33,160
You...

873
00:28:34,560 --> 00:28:34,920
No.

874
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:36,080
No!

875
00:28:38,660 --> 00:28:40,180
(Huairou folks have strength to spare)

876
00:28:40,280 --> 00:28:42,000
Stay here and hold him.

877
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,080
Hold his hat.

878
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:43,760
Hold the hat.

879
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:44,640
No!

880
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:45,360
Bai,

881
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:46,720
I can't stay up here!

882
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:51,160
You scared Chengcheng.

883
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,000
His head isn't flat in the back.

884
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,320
It's round.

885
00:29:02,720 --> 00:29:03,360
How about this?

886
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:04,960
Two people carry me,

887
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:06,000
with someone here

888
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:07,680
holding my upper arm.

889
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:08,880
That should keep me

890
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:09,680
pretty steady.

891
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,880
Someone supports my back.

892
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,600
Once we get there, turn sideways,

893
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:13,200
and we're done.

894
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:13,480
Yeah.

895
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,920
Yeah, that could work.

896
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:15,360
Let's go.

897
00:29:15,360 --> 00:29:16,000
You stay behind.

898
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:17,320
I'll handle his arms.

899
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,280
Watch the hat.

900
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:20,120
(Claiming the hat position)
Give me a hand too.

901
00:29:21,080 --> 00:29:23,000
(Not a chance)
Only Bing and I can handle the hat.

902
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,240
No one else can do it.

903
00:29:24,780 --> 00:29:26,380
(Plan foiled)

904
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:28,040
Come on, let's try lifting him.

905
00:29:28,320 --> 00:29:28,680
Come on.

906
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:29,420
(Leave the sabotage to me)

907
00:29:30,860 --> 00:29:31,940
(Sabotage spot taken)

908
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:33,400
Come on. One, two.

909
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,200
(Look at that gap)

910
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,040
That's too high.

911
00:29:37,040 --> 00:29:38,600
Who can reach the hat?

912
00:29:38,600 --> 00:29:39,240
Too high.

913
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:40,320
Look.

914
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:41,200
Here, go ahead.

915
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,400
Can you carry me, Churan?

916
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:50,640
(The perfect chance)

917
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:50,960
Come on.

918
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:54,160
You sure you can?

919
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:54,480
Yes.

920
00:29:58,340 --> 00:29:59,680
(Still nowhere near high enough)

921
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:01,040
No. Use your elbows, Teng.

922
00:30:01,040 --> 00:30:01,640
Elbows.

923
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:04,880
My dear old dad.

924
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:05,760
(Wriggling around)

925
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:07,680
Teng.

926
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:09,600
Teng.

927
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:10,440
Poor Lin's under so much pressure.

928
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,820
(Caught in the middle)

929
00:30:12,900 --> 00:30:15,420
(One moment we're close,
the next we're far apart)

930
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,520
We need someone else

931
00:30:18,520 --> 00:30:19,960
just to support Teng.

932
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:22,560
Let me ask you.

933
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,440
With him carrying you,

934
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:26,160
aren't you basically an extra head?

935
00:30:26,620 --> 00:30:27,840
(Before and after)

936
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:29,800
Why not sit on his shoulders?

937
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:31,920
I can do that.

938
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:33,360
Lin, can I sit on your shoulders?

939
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:34,360
Sure.

940
00:30:34,360 --> 00:30:35,640
We just need

941
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:36,960
to reach that height to steady the hat.

942
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,080
Put him down first.

943
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:39,400
Okay, put him down.

944
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:40,360
First...

945
00:30:40,360 --> 00:30:41,520
Let's get Teng up there first.

946
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:43,120
Yeah.

947
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,520
Let's figure out how to lift Teng.

948
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:45,240
I don't matter.

949
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:45,920
Same thing.

950
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:47,080
Same method.

951
00:30:47,560 --> 00:30:48,280
I need two people to carry me.

952
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:49,560
Two people to carry him...

953
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:50,400
Yeah, you pick.

954
00:30:52,760 --> 00:30:53,680
That's a tough choice.

955
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:55,760
Carry me.

956
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:58,520
We each take one

957
00:30:58,520 --> 00:30:59,120
of Teng's legs.

958
00:30:59,120 --> 00:30:59,840
You carry my leg?

959
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:00,560
You carry...

960
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:02,400
No, just hold his waist.

961
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,160
We'll carry him.

962
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:03,880
Teng's getting older.

963
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:05,240
He can't handle your antics.

964
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:06,680
What if you try to win the game

965
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:07,880
and drop him?

966
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:11,000
That'd be the end of us.

967
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:15,160
Can I politely ask?

968
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,560
Are they even looking
for the Impostors anymore?

969
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:18,060
(Haven't done
the actual challenge at all)

970
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:18,960
How about this?

971
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:21,200
I'll support Teng's
waist for the first half.

972
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,520
Then, for the second half,

973
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:23,840
I'll push Jingyu's hip into the circle.

974
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:24,320
Yeah. Come on.

975
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,960
I'll handle the hat. Let's go.

976
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:27,280
(Both Impostors secure spots by the hat)

977
00:31:27,280 --> 00:31:28,480
Wait, Lin, how are you carrying him?

978
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:28,960
Like this.

979
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:31,280
Let's go.

980
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,320
I'm pretty light, right?

981
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:34,720
Yep.

982
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:36,680
Wait, first...

983
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:37,480
The hat...

984
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:37,800
Come on.

985
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:39,480
One, two, three, go.

986
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:41,080
(Missed it)
Three, go.

987
00:31:44,020 --> 00:31:47,780
(Way beyond elbow reach)

988
00:31:47,820 --> 00:31:50,060
(Grabbing at thin air)

989
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,480
Get lower!

990
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:53,280
Lower!

991
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:54,640
Your torso...

992
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:56,160
Your torso's so long!

993
00:31:58,940 --> 00:32:01,000
(Getting higher and higher)

994
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:01,640
No!

995
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:08,480
Why am I so much shorter?

996
00:32:08,860 --> 00:32:11,020
(I'm over 180 cm tall, you know)

997
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:13,320
Why's there such a huge gap?

998
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:15,520
Are we doing something wrong?

999
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:17,160
Why's the gap so big?

1000
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:17,840
Teng,

1001
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:18,520
he can go limp,

1002
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:19,320
but you can't.

1003
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:20,720
(Wrongly accused)
I wasn't.

1004
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:21,120
I wasn't going limp.

1005
00:32:21,120 --> 00:32:21,680
Are you going limp?

1006
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,320
I'm stretching up
and still can't reach him.

1007
00:32:23,760 --> 00:32:24,960
Bing, you're blaming the wrong guy.

1008
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:26,400
He's standing perfectly straight.

1009
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,880
He really can't reach.

1010
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:29,160
We...

1011
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:30,400
We'll hold his calves.

1012
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:31,680
You guys have him

1013
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:32,360
up this high.

1014
00:32:32,360 --> 00:32:33,120
We should just

1015
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:34,920
let him stand here.

1016
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:36,000
Right there?

1017
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:36,880
Otherwise, when we get there,

1018
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:37,680
he won't reach.

1019
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:39,160
He needs that extra height.

1020
00:32:39,400 --> 00:32:40,480
Yeah. Just hold his calves.

1021
00:32:40,480 --> 00:32:41,800
Then you can reach, right?

1022
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:42,720
Wanna give it a shot?

1023
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:43,040
Let's go.

1024
00:32:43,280 --> 00:32:44,040
Three, two.

1025
00:32:45,760 --> 00:32:47,360
Why are you sitting
on my shoulders again?

1026
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:49,360
What else am I supposed to do?

1027
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:50,920
Straighten up a bit.

1028
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:51,360
Yeah.

1029
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:52,120
(Standing tall and proud)

1030
00:32:52,120 --> 00:32:52,680
I'm telling you.

1031
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:54,080
No, if you sit on his shoulders,

1032
00:32:54,080 --> 00:32:54,760
it's easier for you.

1033
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:56,240
But not for you if I sit on yours.

1034
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:56,640
Yeah.

1035
00:32:56,640 --> 00:32:58,200
He needs to sit
on your shoulders for more height.

1036
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,600
We can't just hold him like this.

1037
00:32:59,880 --> 00:33:00,800
No, just...

1038
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,120
Both of you hold up my feet.

1039
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,120
Dare to try?

1040
00:33:03,120 --> 00:33:03,880
Wouldn't that be higher?

1041
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:04,920
See?

1042
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,240
Quick, come on!

1043
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:07,800
Come on!

1044
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:09,400
Go!

1045
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,160
Quick!

1046
00:33:10,160 --> 00:33:10,880
Go!

1047
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:11,760
Go!

1048
00:33:11,760 --> 00:33:12,360
Quick!

1049
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:13,240
The balls.

1050
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:15,080
(More rushing, more chaos)
Quick. Lift.

1051
00:33:16,280 --> 00:33:17,680
Churan, could you go any slower?

1052
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:19,320
Churan, take your sweet time.

1053
00:33:20,280 --> 00:33:21,360
Churan, support Teng.

1054
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:22,040
I'm worried he'll get hurt.

1055
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:23,000
Come on, I'll support Teng.

1056
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:24,320
You stay behind.

1057
00:33:25,080 --> 00:33:25,600
One, two.

1058
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:26,480
Go.

1059
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:29,870
(Almost there)
Go a little more limp.

1060
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:30,280
Slow down.

1061
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:31,360
Go limp.

1062
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:33,000
Can you go a little more limp?

1063
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:36,640
(Manually making him go limp)
Come on. Three, two, one.

1064
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:37,400
Start.

1065
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:39,080
Go.

1066
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,400
Careful.

1067
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:41,800
How could the Impostors sabotage this?

1068
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:43,800
How could they have the heart?

1069
00:33:49,100 --> 00:33:50,420
(Airborne handrail)

1070
00:33:50,440 --> 00:33:51,640
Teng.

1071
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:53,520
(Forcing it into position)

1072
00:33:53,520 --> 00:33:54,560
Lean toward me.

1073
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:55,760
Teng, stop grabbing me.

1074
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,120
Lean toward me.

1075
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:58,240
Teng, stop grabbing me.

1076
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:01,560
A little faster.

1077
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:02,840
You guys okay over there?

1078
00:34:03,060 --> 00:34:04,160
(Face full of pain)

1079
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:05,080
Lean toward me.

1080
00:34:11,700 --> 00:34:13,940
(Today's workout: Holding up 45 kg)

1081
00:34:15,560 --> 00:34:16,190
Hurry.

1082
00:34:16,660 --> 00:34:18,420
(Sneaking to the right)

1083
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:19,400
Teng.

1084
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,320
(Gradually shifting
into a side-by-side formation)

1085
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:21,920
Teng.

1086
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:23,000
You two, move right.

1087
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:23,360
A little right.

1088
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:24,040
Both of you, move right.

1089
00:34:24,040 --> 00:34:24,440
Right.

1090
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:25,360
Yeah, you two. Right.

1091
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:26,190
Further right.

1092
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:27,190
Teng.

1093
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:28,530
(Not budging)
You two, move right.

1094
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:29,560
No.

1095
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:30,710
(Still not budging)
Chengcheng, move right.

1096
00:34:30,710 --> 00:34:31,190
A little right.

1097
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:32,400
Right.

1098
00:34:33,230 --> 00:34:34,080
Who's pulling on Huang Jingyu?

1099
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:34,600
Who is it?

1100
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:36,800
Teng.

1101
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,520
Teng.

1102
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:40,880
Teng, stop pulling.

1103
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:43,320
(Trying so hard, pulling even harder)
Stop pulling him.

1104
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,280
Teng, stop pulling.

1105
00:34:44,280 --> 00:34:45,440
(Double the weight)

1106
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:46,320
Stop pulling him!

1107
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:49,000
(Total chaos)
I'm moving right.

1108
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,230
Where's my camera?

1109
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:53,600
I'm over here.

1110
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:57,920
Stop pulling him!

1111
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,080
I'm completely out of the shot!

1112
00:35:01,680 --> 00:35:02,400
Two fell out.

1113
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,960
(Eight balls left)
Chengcheng, put some muscle into it.

1114
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:05,960
Where's my camera?

1115
00:35:07,680 --> 00:35:08,280
Teng.

1116
00:35:08,300 --> 00:35:10,900
(Holding on for dear life)

1117
00:35:13,940 --> 00:35:14,960
(Barely squeezing through)

1118
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,880
I'm completely out of the shot.

1119
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:17,920
No.

1120
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,280
Slow down.

1121
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:20,400
You guys up front, slow down.

1122
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:21,520
Teng.

1123
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:31,040
Teng.

1124
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,800
Impostor. Teng.

1125
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:33,220
(Slipping down)

1126
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:34,800
Impostor. Teng.

1127
00:35:35,060 --> 00:35:36,780
(Slid all the way down to his chest)

1128
00:35:37,680 --> 00:35:38,760
Definitely an Impostor.

1129
00:35:39,500 --> 00:35:40,660
(Trying his absolute hardest)

1130
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:42,200
Are you...

1131
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:45,180
(Is saving the hat really worth it?)
Are you really here to help me?

1132
00:35:52,240 --> 00:35:52,800
I can't!

1133
00:35:58,120 --> 00:35:59,780
(The human piggyback ride has collapsed)
How'd I end up down here?

1134
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,080
How'd I fall off?

1135
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:04,040
We can just walk ourselves.

1136
00:36:10,380 --> 00:36:11,700
(The fake Impostor is trying so hard)

1137
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:22,000
Hurry up!

1138
00:36:27,660 --> 00:36:31,620
(Going after his collar again)

1139
00:36:46,820 --> 00:36:47,780
(Why's he trying harder than us?)

1140
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:49,540
(Refusing to let go)

1141
00:36:52,740 --> 00:36:55,420
(An Impostor forced to work hard)

1142
00:37:17,220 --> 00:37:19,780
(The hat protector finally arrives)

1143
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,400
Only three balls left.

1144
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:22,240
Mission failed.

1145
00:37:22,300 --> 00:37:24,260
(Mission failed)

1146
00:37:25,580 --> 00:37:27,780
(Another intense workout done)

1147
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,280
It's definitely him!

1148
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:34,520
For sure.

1149
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:37,780
I even managed to save three balls.

1150
00:37:37,780 --> 00:37:38,940
(I worked that hard,
and you still suspect me?)

1151
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:40,200
Definitely.

1152
00:37:40,600 --> 00:37:41,640
It's definitely him.

1153
00:37:44,640 --> 00:37:45,600
Northernmost Beijing.

1154
00:37:46,560 --> 00:37:47,640
Northernmost Beijing.

1155
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:50,680
Bai never wants to come home again.

1156
00:37:51,780 --> 00:37:55,060
(Beautiful Huairou)

1157
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:55,520
Bai.

1158
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:58,080
He's never been this tired coming home.

1159
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:00,360
This was supposed
to be a mental challenge.

1160
00:38:00,360 --> 00:38:00,720
Exactly.

1161
00:38:01,160 --> 00:38:02,200
How'd it become a workout?

1162
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:07,760
I can't lift

1163
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:08,560
my elbows anymore.

1164
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,640
Don't be surprised if next month

1165
00:38:10,640 --> 00:38:11,800
Churan goes viral for weightlifting.

1166
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:15,840
She'll have muscles twice as big.

1167
00:38:18,280 --> 00:38:20,160
After that last round,

1168
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:21,880
I feel like I could go rock climbing.

1169
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:24,080
Seriously.

1170
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,520
My joints feel so strong now.

1171
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:27,800
Sure, you can go rock climbing,

1172
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:29,200
as long as two strong guys

1173
00:38:29,200 --> 00:38:30,040
hold up your legs.

1174
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:31,560
And climb with me, right?

1175
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:32,320
(Reaching the top with lots of help)

1176
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:33,960
Come on. I wanna grab that one.

1177
00:38:35,120 --> 00:38:36,480
A three-man climbing pyramid.

1178
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,460
(More like a three-man climbing team)

1179
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:41,240
Everyone,

1180
00:38:41,240 --> 00:38:42,600
you failed that last round.

1181
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:44,440
But if you vote out an Impostor now,

1182
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,280
the innocent team can still win.

1183
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:49,100
(Leaving the innocent team)
Just vote me out.

1184
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:57,120
I'll go with you, Bai.

1185
00:38:57,120 --> 00:38:58,640
Everyone at the back was fooling around.

1186
00:38:58,640 --> 00:38:59,440
I was just following along.

1187
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,500
(Carrying the burden alone)

1188
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:04,040
Up there, all I could think was...

1189
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:06,680
Teng's gonna pull me down.

1190
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:09,320
(Main suspect:)
I'm definitely innocent, Bing.

1191
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:11,000
We worked so hard on that hat.

1192
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:11,760
We did great last round.

1193
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:12,720
And this round too.

1194
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:13,600
Here's the thing.

1195
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:14,880
All I wanted was

1196
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:16,360
for Jingyu to lean against me.

1197
00:39:17,280 --> 00:39:18,200
You could've said something.

1198
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:19,320
Just say, Jingyu, lean this way.

1199
00:39:19,600 --> 00:39:20,680
I couldn't even speak.

1200
00:39:21,520 --> 00:39:22,840
I really couldn't talk.

1201
00:39:23,120 --> 00:39:24,040
You were too busy grabbing him.

1202
00:39:24,900 --> 00:39:26,980
(What an interesting turn of events)

1203
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:28,800
Teng, the entire time,

1204
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:30,320
you actually supported me

1205
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:32,080
for five seconds at most.

1206
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:32,800
The rest was just pulling.

1207
00:39:33,560 --> 00:39:35,760
You nearly tore me in half.

1208
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:38,160
I even stepped on that thing

1209
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:39,730
(I swear I'm innocent)
trying to climb back up.

1210
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:40,360
Then why

1211
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:41,840
did you keep pulling me backward?

1212
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:43,880
I had nothing to hold on to!

1213
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:45,800
I couldn't climb back up!

1214
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:50,440
You pulled me up?

1215
00:39:51,080 --> 00:39:52,080
You were pulling me down!

1216
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:54,640
No, back then,

1217
00:39:54,640 --> 00:39:57,080
I felt like you were deliberately

1218
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:59,320
tilting your head down

1219
00:39:59,320 --> 00:40:00,120
to spill the balls.

1220
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:01,500
(Teng's suspect)
Me?

1221
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:03,360
Don't you think
your pulling caused that?

1222
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:04,560
No, I had to pull.

1223
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:05,760
It was like climbing a chimney.

1224
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:06,360
I had to climb up.

1225
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:08,000
I needed something to grab, you know?

1226
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Of course I had to pull hard.

1227
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:09,920
Otherwise, I'd fall.

1228
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,400
Wait. You broke the rules.

1229
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:12,560
What rule did I break?

1230
00:40:12,560 --> 00:40:13,680
You were supposed to stay limp.

1231
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:15,840
Why are you arguing with me?

1232
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:16,360
If you grab him

1233
00:40:16,360 --> 00:40:17,200
and he goes along with it,

1234
00:40:17,200 --> 00:40:18,320
won't he fall backward?

1235
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:20,320
(Can't he trust me to catch him?)
I wanted him to lean back against me.

1236
00:40:20,520 --> 00:40:20,960
No way.

1237
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:22,200
It was too high. I was scared.

1238
00:40:22,200 --> 00:40:22,800
That height...

1239
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:24,260
(Feeling wronged.gif)

1240
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:25,160
But seriously,

1241
00:40:25,160 --> 00:40:26,640
there's one thing I don't get.

1242
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:27,480
Whether Teng was pulling or not,

1243
00:40:27,480 --> 00:40:28,080
I can understand that.

1244
00:40:28,080 --> 00:40:29,080
It was just

1245
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:30,160
a survival instinct.

1246
00:40:30,160 --> 00:40:30,840
What I don't get

1247
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:32,000
is why you didn't let Li Yunrui

1248
00:40:32,140 --> 00:40:32,920
(Lightweight rider)
ride instead.

1249
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:33,360
Or let

1250
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:35,360
me ride.

1251
00:40:35,880 --> 00:40:36,640
Sit where?

1252
00:40:36,640 --> 00:40:38,160
Up there, above his head.

1253
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:39,720
I don't trust any of you.

1254
00:40:39,720 --> 00:40:40,640
Why would I let you ride?

1255
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:41,760
I'm guarding the hat.

1256
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:43,320
For that job, first,

1257
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:44,400
you need someone innocent.

1258
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:44,880
Second,

1259
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:45,880
they need the skills.

1260
00:40:45,980 --> 00:40:47,760
(Skills at yanking people?)

1261
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:48,760
I know myself.

1262
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:49,840
I've got both.

1263
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:51,640
Except maybe Bing.

1264
00:40:52,440 --> 00:40:53,520
I trust Bing.

1265
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:54,480
Only the two of us

1266
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:55,200
are innocent

1267
00:40:55,200 --> 00:40:56,440
and can keep that hat steady.

1268
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:56,760
Seriously,

1269
00:40:56,760 --> 00:40:57,480
after that round,

1270
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,280
my sloping shoulders

1271
00:40:58,280 --> 00:40:59,480
are practically square now.

1272
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:02,680
Now I know

1273
00:41:02,680 --> 00:41:04,160
why I kept sliding down.

1274
00:41:06,200 --> 00:41:08,520
I've finally figured it out.

1275
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:09,840
Let's do another round
on my right shoulder.

1276
00:41:10,020 --> 00:41:11,320
(Square shoulders in no time)

1277
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:12,040
A few more rides,

1278
00:41:12,040 --> 00:41:13,240
and you'll be a model.

1279
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:16,960
I suspect Chengcheng and Churan.

1280
00:41:16,980 --> 00:41:17,880
(An Impostor starts pointing fingers)

1281
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:18,920
Churan kept...

1282
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:20,400
I found it really weird.

1283
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,880
Wasn't the human prop

1284
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:22,640
on our left?

1285
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:25,080
But Churan kept saying
"move to the right",

1286
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:26,120
"move to the right".

1287
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,920
Chengcheng was on my right.

1288
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:29,440
Our butts were already touching.

1289
00:41:29,440 --> 00:41:31,280
And she kept saying "move to the right".

1290
00:41:31,960 --> 00:41:33,400
Lin was practically riding

1291
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:33,960
the human prop.

1292
00:41:34,480 --> 00:41:36,000
Yeah, I really was sitting on him.

1293
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:37,320
(Thanks, Mr. Huang)

1294
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:37,880
No.

1295
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:40,400
I couldn't see anything.

1296
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:41,640
(Quick to defend himself)
Teng's butt was here.

1297
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:43,160
Yours was here.

1298
00:41:43,160 --> 00:41:43,760
Moving sideways.

1299
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:45,160
I couldn't even see the camera.

1300
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:46,160
I wasn't even in the shot.

1301
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:49,640
But I really was trying.

1302
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:51,600
By the end,

1303
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:53,400
my left arm was completely numb.

1304
00:41:53,400 --> 00:41:54,400
Even my butt was numb.

1305
00:41:54,400 --> 00:41:55,600
Then I saw you stepping there,

1306
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:56,480
so I rushed back to help.

1307
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:58,320
But everyone was laughing so hard

1308
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:59,800
they could barely stand.

1309
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,680
So I got down.

1310
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:05,800
I think Churan's directions

1311
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:06,440
were suspicious.

1312
00:42:06,780 --> 00:42:07,800
(Pointing fingers at the one
who gave directions)

1313
00:42:07,800 --> 00:42:09,560
Because Teng's whole body

1314
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:10,960
was leaning sideways.

1315
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:12,850
(Let me explain)
He was leaning toward Chengcheng.

1316
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:14,400
Chengcheng was on the outside,

1317
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:15,520
so he had to walk faster.

1318
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:16,440
That's why I told him to hurry.

1319
00:42:16,440 --> 00:42:17,840
When I was leaning over,

1320
00:42:17,840 --> 00:42:18,560
what were you doing?

1321
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,040
Pulling you back.

1322
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:22,640
Pulling me back

1323
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:23,600
or pulling me down?

1324
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:24,600
Back.

1325
00:42:26,360 --> 00:42:26,960
I was pulling you back.

1326
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:30,320
I really think...

1327
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:31,680
I just think it's those two.

1328
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:33,400
I really suspect both of them.

1329
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:34,480
It's not me.

1330
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:37,120
I think two
of those three are Impostors.

1331
00:42:37,500 --> 00:42:39,060
(Teng's suspect list)

1332
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:39,960
All right, everyone.

1333
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:41,400
If there's nothing else to add,

1334
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:42,440
let's vote.

1335
00:42:44,900 --> 00:42:45,900
(Li Yunrui: 2, Shen Teng: 3,
Wang Churan: 2)

1336
00:42:45,900 --> 00:42:47,620
(Shen Teng: 3 votes, out)

1337
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:48,320
Number five got three?

1338
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:50,200
What?

1339
00:42:51,440 --> 00:42:51,960
Teng

1340
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:52,840
is eliminated.

1341
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:54,760
I'm out?

1342
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:03,680
Who voted for me? Let's see.

1343
00:43:04,120 --> 00:43:04,800
Which ones?

1344
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:06,440
One.

1345
00:43:06,440 --> 00:43:06,840
Who else?

1346
00:43:07,280 --> 00:43:08,520
Two, three.

1347
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:11,920
Only three? That can't be right.

1348
00:43:13,040 --> 00:43:13,600
Three.

1349
00:43:13,880 --> 00:43:14,840
I voted for number seven.

1350
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:17,560
Just three?

1351
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,560
I only got three votes?

1352
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:19,520
Yeah, the most votes.

1353
00:43:26,320 --> 00:43:26,960
You guys have fun.

1354
00:43:29,280 --> 00:43:30,160
He's hurt.

1355
00:43:30,540 --> 00:43:32,880
(After everything I did...)

1356
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:33,600
Stop pulling him.

1357
00:43:39,440 --> 00:43:40,920
Teng

1358
00:43:41,560 --> 00:43:42,040
was innocent.

1359
00:43:42,520 --> 00:43:42,920
What?

1360
00:43:43,720 --> 00:43:44,120
What?

1361
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:48,560
Innocent?

1362
00:43:54,120 --> 00:43:55,640
My role? WeTV subscriber.

1363
00:43:59,020 --> 00:44:00,600
(Even our most confident round
went wrong)

1364
00:44:00,600 --> 00:44:01,720
He was innocent?

1365
00:44:04,680 --> 00:44:05,920
Such a hardworking innocent guy.

1366
00:44:05,940 --> 00:44:08,580
You idiots!

1367
00:44:13,080 --> 00:44:14,520
I can't believe you voted me out.

1368
00:44:15,440 --> 00:44:16,400
After all these years,
this is the first time

1369
00:44:16,400 --> 00:44:17,680
I've seen him get
this heated over a game.

1370
00:44:18,380 --> 00:44:19,760
(Grinding his back teeth in frustration)

1371
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:21,560
In a game that's all about talking,

1372
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:23,200
voting out the wrong person

1373
00:44:23,200 --> 00:44:24,720
doesn't make you feel that guilty.

1374
00:44:25,280 --> 00:44:26,280
But after someone worked so hard,

1375
00:44:26,280 --> 00:44:27,080
you still voted him out.

1376
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:28,760
Teng.

1377
00:44:28,760 --> 00:44:30,320
He even climbed on top of someone.

1378
00:44:30,320 --> 00:44:31,320
And you still voted him out.

1379
00:44:34,120 --> 00:44:35,480
Why are you so worked up?

1380
00:44:35,480 --> 00:44:36,760
Didn't you vote for Teng too?

1381
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:37,520
Yeah.

1382
00:44:38,240 --> 00:44:40,400
If I hadn't watched you guys vote,

1383
00:44:40,400 --> 00:44:42,240
I'd actually be touched.

1384
00:44:46,640 --> 00:44:48,320
The Impostors were Chengcheng and Lin.

1385
00:44:48,760 --> 00:44:50,000
Since you voted wrong both times,

1386
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:51,960
the Impostors win.

1387
00:44:58,560 --> 00:44:59,400
You know what Li Yunrui is?

1388
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:00,200
A wolf in sheep's clothing.

1389
00:45:00,640 --> 00:45:02,200
He smiles while plotting against you.

1390
00:45:02,680 --> 00:45:04,240
There are knives behind that smile.

1391
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:07,240
Seriously,

1392
00:45:07,240 --> 00:45:08,280
I didn't sabotage a thing.

1393
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:09,960
I gave it my all.

1394
00:45:09,960 --> 00:45:11,560
I carried him with all my heart.

1395
00:45:11,560 --> 00:45:12,360
Pretending to be innocent.

1396
00:45:12,360 --> 00:45:13,160
Kept him steady too.

1397
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:14,920
So we lost by turning on each other?

1398
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:17,200
And

1399
00:45:17,200 --> 00:45:18,400
by picking the right people.

1400
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:21,880
Thanks to Teng

1401
00:45:21,880 --> 00:45:22,800
and Hu.

1402
00:45:23,640 --> 00:45:24,520
One lifted the hat,

1403
00:45:24,520 --> 00:45:26,820
(They each deserve half the credit)
and the other yanked Jingyu.

1404
00:45:26,920 --> 00:45:28,760
Otherwise, they'd
have won way too easily.

1405
00:45:30,280 --> 00:45:31,360
The Impostors

1406
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:32,080
had you carry me

1407
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:32,600
just

1408
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:33,240
to wear

1409
00:45:33,240 --> 00:45:34,200
everyone out.

1410
00:45:34,220 --> 00:45:36,340
(Now that's strategy)

1411
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:37,760
Anyone else would've
been easier to carry.

1412
00:45:37,760 --> 00:45:38,240
Seriously.

1413
00:45:38,920 --> 00:45:40,480
So from now on,

1414
00:45:40,480 --> 00:45:41,880
stop pretending

1415
00:45:41,880 --> 00:45:43,200
you're all fitness experts.

1416
00:45:46,080 --> 00:45:46,920
I'm dead tired.

1417
00:45:48,480 --> 00:45:49,160
Bai

1418
00:45:49,600 --> 00:45:51,160
can't even lift his arms.

1419
00:45:51,700 --> 00:45:54,100
(Completely wiped out)

1420
00:45:55,990 --> 00:45:58,280
Prices go down,
but the fun only goes up.

1421
00:46:06,160 --> 00:46:08,250
Double the beauty.
Leave work stress behind.

1422
00:46:14,720 --> 00:46:15,300
Dress sharp

1423
00:46:15,600 --> 00:46:17,330
and play hard just like me.

1424
00:46:17,510 --> 00:46:20,020
Taobao has everything
you need for every kind of fun.

1425
00:46:20,020 --> 00:46:21,730
Turn up the fun. Start with Taobao.

1426
00:46:21,730 --> 00:46:23,840
Shop Taobao and save more
on Tmall's Double 11.

1427
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:27,360
We've prepared
some pear soup for everyone.

1428
00:46:27,360 --> 00:46:29,360
Get your energy back.

1429
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:30,800
Pear soup.

1430
00:46:47,320 --> 00:46:48,000
Feels amazing.

1431
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:49,200
Perfect weather for a motorcycle ride.

1432
00:46:49,200 --> 00:46:50,680
Especially with this view.

1433
00:46:50,680 --> 00:46:51,160
Yeah.

1434
00:46:57,920 --> 00:46:59,000
Hello, everyone.

1435
00:46:59,280 --> 00:46:59,560
Hello.

1436
00:47:00,640 --> 00:47:01,880
Welcome to Beijing.

1437
00:47:01,880 --> 00:47:03,200
(Chen Rui, PhD in zoology, Chinese Academy of Sciences)
I'd like to introduce you

1438
00:47:03,200 --> 00:47:04,427
(China Scientific Expedition Association Secretary-General)
to one of Beijing's native birds.

1439
00:47:04,427 --> 00:47:05,320
(Head of Shi Tan Ji Scientists Team)
to one of Beijing's native birds.

1440
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:06,240
It's called the chukar.

1441
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:07,840
(Chukar)
It's related to chickens.

1442
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:08,600
Here's a question.

1443
00:47:08,600 --> 00:47:09,680
Does the chukar

1444
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:10,880
change its feather color

1445
00:47:10,880 --> 00:47:12,280
during Beijing's beautiful,

1446
00:47:12,280 --> 00:47:13,960
color-changing autumn?

1447
00:47:13,960 --> 00:47:14,280
Yes.

1448
00:47:14,280 --> 00:47:14,900
Then it's a yes.

1449
00:47:14,900 --> 00:47:15,600
(Figuring out his question style)

1450
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:16,720
It's definitely a yes.

1451
00:47:17,240 --> 00:47:17,800
Okay.

1452
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:18,480
Your answer

1453
00:47:18,480 --> 00:47:19,080
is wrong.

1454
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:20,680
A perfect example of what not to do.

1455
00:47:20,680 --> 00:47:21,920
What a trick question.

1456
00:47:21,920 --> 00:47:23,840
Chukars don't actually change color.

1457
00:47:23,840 --> 00:47:25,840
But they have a relative in the Arctic

1458
00:47:25,840 --> 00:47:26,520
that does.

1459
00:47:26,520 --> 00:47:27,680
It looks very similar

1460
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:29,400
and is called the rock ptarmigan.

1461
00:47:29,420 --> 00:47:30,400
(Spring and summer. Footage from the internet)

1462
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:31,560
(Rock ptarmigan, a Class II protected animal in China.)
It changes its look every season.

1463
00:47:31,560 --> 00:47:31,960
(Autumn)

1464
00:47:31,960 --> 00:47:33,120
(Mainly in Northern Hemisphere mountains and tundra.)
It's a camouflage strategy.

1465
00:47:33,140 --> 00:47:34,080
(Feathers change color with the seasons. Winter)

1466
00:47:34,080 --> 00:47:36,400
But chukars stay the same color year-round.

1467
00:47:36,600 --> 00:47:38,040
They often live around

1468
00:47:38,040 --> 00:47:39,760
granite and rocky slopes.

1469
00:47:39,760 --> 00:47:42,040
Their feathers blend right in with the rocks.

1470
00:47:42,040 --> 00:47:43,240
That's camouflage too.

1471
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:44,640
In the next challenge,

1472
00:47:44,640 --> 00:47:45,920
you'll need to work

1473
00:47:45,920 --> 00:47:47,360
with your teammates to cover for each other.

1474
00:47:47,360 --> 00:47:49,560
Just like chukars hiding among rocks,

1475
00:47:49,560 --> 00:47:50,560
you must avoid being spotted.

1476
00:47:50,720 --> 00:47:51,360
Okay!

1477
00:47:52,280 --> 00:47:53,480
Our next challenge

1478
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:55,240
is called AI Q&A.

1479
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:58,120
(AI Q&A)
You'll split into two teams of four.

1480
00:47:58,120 --> 00:47:59,840
Each team takes turns

1481
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:01,200
presenting and guessing.

1482
00:48:01,560 --> 00:48:02,760
(AI Q&A: Presenting team)
The presenting team gets

1483
00:48:02,760 --> 00:48:03,640
an AI-generated

1484
00:48:03,640 --> 00:48:04,200
response to a scenario.

1485
00:48:04,720 --> 00:48:06,720
They must discuss

1486
00:48:06,720 --> 00:48:07,800
and pick one member

1487
00:48:07,800 --> 00:48:09,680
to present the actual AI response.

1488
00:48:09,680 --> 00:48:11,320
The other three members

1489
00:48:11,320 --> 00:48:13,680
must use the same scenario

1490
00:48:13,680 --> 00:48:15,680
and imitate the AI's style,

1491
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:16,880
making up their own responses

1492
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:18,080
to cover for their teammate.

1493
00:48:18,520 --> 00:48:20,600
The presenting team can choose

1494
00:48:20,600 --> 00:48:22,920
anyone from the guessing team
as a partner.

1495
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:24,680
(Guessing team)
The guessing team watches the performances

1496
00:48:24,680 --> 00:48:26,920
and decides which member

1497
00:48:26,920 --> 00:48:28,880
gave the real AI response.

1498
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:30,600
If they guess correctly on the first try,

1499
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:31,200
they get three points.

1500
00:48:31,560 --> 00:48:33,120
On the second try, one point.

1501
00:48:33,120 --> 00:48:35,280
The team with more points wins.

1502
00:48:35,520 --> 00:48:36,600
Got it.

1503
00:48:36,820 --> 00:48:37,980
(He actually understood the rules?)

1504
00:48:40,440 --> 00:48:41,920
So basically...

1505
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:45,000
We're in teams of four.

1506
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:45,640
Correct.

1507
00:48:45,640 --> 00:48:46,720
One person

1508
00:48:47,560 --> 00:48:48,480
gets the actual

1509
00:48:48,480 --> 00:48:49,680
AI-generated response.

1510
00:48:50,120 --> 00:48:51,440
The other three

1511
00:48:51,440 --> 00:48:52,600
have to cover for them

1512
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:53,880
so the other team can't tell

1513
00:48:53,880 --> 00:48:55,320
who has the real AI response.

1514
00:48:56,580 --> 00:48:57,820
(You're a genius)

1515
00:48:58,380 --> 00:48:59,820
(So so)

1516
00:49:01,680 --> 00:49:03,640
Just being here in Bai's hometown

1517
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:04,440
(Back to Bai again)
feels great.

1518
00:49:04,980 --> 00:49:06,820
(Good thing I dressed simply today)

1519
00:49:08,160 --> 00:49:09,800
Bai, why don't you split us into teams?

1520
00:49:10,320 --> 00:49:11,240
Same as always.

1521
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:12,280
Down the middle.

1522
00:49:12,280 --> 00:49:13,080
Split down the middle.

1523
00:49:13,140 --> 00:49:14,520
(Keeping the tradition alive)

1524
00:49:14,520 --> 00:49:15,440
Which team goes first?

1525
00:49:19,680 --> 00:49:20,600
We've got newcomers here.

1526
00:49:20,600 --> 00:49:21,360
Let him watch and learn.

1527
00:49:21,360 --> 00:49:22,280
Otherwise, he won't know

1528
00:49:22,280 --> 00:49:23,640
how far we take things here.

1529
00:49:23,640 --> 00:49:24,520
How far? I'm already...

1530
00:49:24,780 --> 00:49:25,880
(Don't scare me)

1531
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:27,400
You've got me shaking.

1532
00:49:27,400 --> 00:49:29,200
Bai, you guys do a practice round.

1533
00:49:29,200 --> 00:49:30,240
Show us how it's done.

1534
00:49:30,240 --> 00:49:30,920
Sure. Let's go.

1535
00:49:31,220 --> 00:49:31,900
(Practice round:
Presenting team vs. guessing team)

1536
00:49:31,900 --> 00:49:32,700
(Scenario: You haven't seen
each other for days after a fight)

1537
00:49:32,700 --> 00:49:33,280
(One night, you knock on their door)

1538
00:49:33,280 --> 00:49:35,200
(Say something to soften their heart)
We pick one person to act this out,

1539
00:49:35,230 --> 00:49:36,240
(And end the silent treatment)
right?

1540
00:49:36,760 --> 00:49:37,640
All four have to act.

1541
00:49:37,640 --> 00:49:38,400
(This is gonna be tough)
Oh my God.

1542
00:49:38,400 --> 00:49:41,120
No, we pick one person to perform

1543
00:49:41,120 --> 00:49:42,040
the AI response shown here.

1544
00:49:42,040 --> 00:49:43,320
But they can't know the scenario, right?

1545
00:49:43,320 --> 00:49:44,560
Otherwise, they'll guess it.

1546
00:49:44,560 --> 00:49:45,580
(Even more confused)
What are we playing?

1547
00:49:47,320 --> 00:49:48,920
Then what are we supposed to guess?

1548
00:49:49,060 --> 00:49:51,340
(Hu's confusion has taken over)

1549
00:49:51,360 --> 00:49:52,120
Hu.

1550
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:53,980
(A word of advice from Huang)
You can't play a cop, Hu!

1551
00:49:54,640 --> 00:49:56,600
Look how thorough my investigation was.

1552
00:49:56,600 --> 00:49:57,880
(Determined to prove himself)
I cleared everything up beforehand.

1553
00:49:58,600 --> 00:49:59,320
Come on, Hu.

1554
00:49:59,700 --> 00:50:01,060
(Are we being too obvious?)
I'll do it?

1555
00:50:01,240 --> 00:50:01,920
Let's discuss.

1556
00:50:09,120 --> 00:50:09,920
Officer Gao.

1557
00:50:10,220 --> 00:50:11,380
(Mr. Huang's curse)

1558
00:50:11,440 --> 00:50:13,320
Did you get into a fight with a criminal

1559
00:50:13,800 --> 00:50:15,200
and have him hit you

1560
00:50:15,200 --> 00:50:16,080
over the head?

1561
00:50:18,780 --> 00:50:20,380
(A little payback)

1562
00:50:25,380 --> 00:50:26,340
(Can't see a thing)

1563
00:50:26,640 --> 00:50:27,720
Then let's have

1564
00:50:27,720 --> 00:50:29,280
Chief Bai deliver
the AI response.

1565
00:50:29,280 --> 00:50:30,640
(AI performance: Bai Jingting)

1566
00:50:30,640 --> 00:50:31,400
The three of us

1567
00:50:31,400 --> 00:50:33,080
need to sound

1568
00:50:33,080 --> 00:50:34,960
just as emotionless as AI.

1569
00:50:35,360 --> 00:50:36,720
Why are they covering their ears?

1570
00:50:37,120 --> 00:50:38,240
(Who are they blocking out?)
So we can't hear them?

1571
00:50:38,240 --> 00:50:39,480
Why are they covering their own ears?

1572
00:50:40,600 --> 00:50:40,960
Yeah.

1573
00:50:40,960 --> 00:50:42,600
(Manual noise cancellation)
Use fewer filler words.

1574
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:43,680
Sound like AI.

1575
00:50:43,720 --> 00:50:45,840
The officer
has his own special technique.

1576
00:50:48,940 --> 00:50:50,620
(AI performance: Bai Jingting)

1577
00:50:50,620 --> 00:50:51,900
(AI response: I don't need
to argue with you right now)

1578
00:50:51,900 --> 00:50:52,900
(But I can't stand this emotional
distance between us anymore)

1579
00:50:53,040 --> 00:50:53,560
Think of something to say.

1580
00:50:59,560 --> 00:51:00,400
We're ready.

1581
00:51:00,960 --> 00:51:02,200
Let's start with Chief Bai.

1582
00:51:03,040 --> 00:51:03,440
Show us how.

1583
00:51:04,000 --> 00:51:04,520
Set an example.

1584
00:51:04,760 --> 00:51:05,320
Alright, you're up.

1585
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:06,160
Me?

1586
00:51:06,920 --> 00:51:07,800
You picked me.

1587
00:51:08,180 --> 00:51:10,700
(Can't wait)

1588
00:51:11,160 --> 00:51:12,320
I'm at home.

1589
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:13,040
Here's the door.

1590
00:51:14,720 --> 00:51:15,440
You may begin.

1591
00:51:16,420 --> 00:51:17,460
(We've been ignoring each other too long)

1592
00:51:20,580 --> 00:51:23,260
(Will he forgive me?)

1593
00:51:24,860 --> 00:51:26,020
(It's been so long. He looks thinner)

1594
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:50,640
I don't need to argue with you right now.

1595
00:51:52,200 --> 00:51:53,600
There's this emotional distance
between us.

1596
00:51:56,140 --> 00:51:57,140
(What just flew past?)

1597
00:51:58,980 --> 00:52:00,580
(Savoring the moment alone)

1598
00:52:00,840 --> 00:52:01,280
Teng.

1599
00:52:01,820 --> 00:52:04,100
(Love is like a gust of...)

1600
00:52:04,120 --> 00:52:04,600
Wind.

1601
00:52:05,320 --> 00:52:06,760
Wind.

1602
00:52:06,820 --> 00:52:08,460
(His own sound effects)

1603
00:52:08,480 --> 00:52:09,520
I think you've gone crazy.

1604
00:52:09,520 --> 00:52:10,360
Your wind...

1605
00:52:13,460 --> 00:52:17,780
(Feat:)

1606
00:52:24,320 --> 00:52:25,520
Flagging down a truck?

1607
00:52:26,060 --> 00:52:28,140
(Trying to hitch a ride)

1608
00:52:28,240 --> 00:52:29,440
Hey, can you give me a ride?

1609
00:52:29,560 --> 00:52:30,480
Wait, don't leave!

1610
00:52:30,840 --> 00:52:31,520
Taxi!

1611
00:52:32,160 --> 00:52:34,160
Are you heading into town?

1612
00:52:35,880 --> 00:52:37,720
We haven't spoken
in days since our fight.

1613
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:40,600
I just can't take it anymore.

1614
00:52:40,800 --> 00:52:41,520
So I decided

1615
00:52:41,920 --> 00:52:43,120
to come see you tonight.

1616
00:52:43,680 --> 00:52:45,320
I don't want you hurting anymore.

1617
00:52:50,780 --> 00:52:52,780
(Can't hold back the laughter)

1618
00:52:53,080 --> 00:52:54,000
What did you say, Teng?

1619
00:52:54,360 --> 00:52:55,280
I couldn't hear a thing.

1620
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:56,920
Good. That's the point.

1621
00:52:57,920 --> 00:52:59,840
One less chance to laugh at me.

1622
00:53:01,060 --> 00:53:06,020
(But love isn't afraid of ridicule)

1623
00:53:15,840 --> 00:53:16,960
I know you're angry.

1624
00:53:18,480 --> 00:53:19,200
But I think

1625
00:53:19,920 --> 00:53:21,320
we deserve another chance.

1626
00:53:22,880 --> 00:53:24,280
Another chance.

1627
00:53:24,380 --> 00:53:25,900
(Does that sound a little too AI?)

1628
00:53:26,720 --> 00:53:27,680
I think it's Hu.

1629
00:53:27,840 --> 00:53:28,600
I haven't even performed!

1630
00:53:28,600 --> 00:53:29,720
He hasn't gone yet!

1631
00:53:31,680 --> 00:53:33,040
Show some respect!

1632
00:53:35,280 --> 00:53:36,160
Seriously.

1633
00:53:36,160 --> 00:53:38,120
You really won't give up

1634
00:53:38,120 --> 00:53:39,720
on coming after me.

1635
00:53:39,720 --> 00:53:40,400
Hu!

1636
00:53:40,400 --> 00:53:41,680
Wang Churan!

1637
00:53:42,560 --> 00:53:44,440
(Still set on Churan)
No, let him perform first.

1638
00:53:44,440 --> 00:53:45,200
Then we'll vote for you.

1639
00:53:45,720 --> 00:53:46,560
Are you still performing?

1640
00:53:47,340 --> 00:53:48,740
(Let the show begin)

1641
00:53:51,840 --> 00:53:52,760
There's a door code?

1642
00:53:56,240 --> 00:53:56,720
Bing.

1643
00:54:00,280 --> 00:54:01,040
I don't know

1644
00:54:01,960 --> 00:54:02,600
what happened before,

1645
00:54:03,200 --> 00:54:04,280
who was right or wrong.

1646
00:54:04,280 --> 00:54:04,880
But I do know

1647
00:54:05,520 --> 00:54:06,800
that staying apart these past few days

1648
00:54:06,800 --> 00:54:07,520
was definitely wrong.

1649
00:54:10,900 --> 00:54:12,660
(Painfully cheesy)

1650
00:54:16,800 --> 00:54:18,360
Okay, AI. You may leave.

1651
00:54:20,520 --> 00:54:21,800
That line from Jingyu

1652
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:22,720
was either written by AI

1653
00:54:22,720 --> 00:54:24,560
or taken straight from

1654
00:54:24,560 --> 00:54:25,520
his latest drama.

1655
00:54:25,520 --> 00:54:25,960
I'm telling you.

1656
00:54:26,220 --> 00:54:27,720
(Too clever to go unsuspected)

1657
00:54:27,720 --> 00:54:29,240
I'd be shocked if that wasn't AI.

1658
00:54:30,720 --> 00:54:31,600
I feel like Jingyu

1659
00:54:31,600 --> 00:54:32,880
would actually say something like that.

1660
00:54:33,140 --> 00:54:34,480
(Reputation under attack)

1661
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:36,200
Fan Chengcheng, stop roasting me on TV.

1662
00:54:45,560 --> 00:54:46,520
I think I've figured it out.

1663
00:54:46,520 --> 00:54:47,060
(Her sixth sense strikes again)

1664
00:54:47,480 --> 00:54:48,880
You've got a feeling again?

1665
00:54:48,880 --> 00:54:50,320
You're acting pretty mystical today.

1666
00:54:50,320 --> 00:54:50,720
Seriously.

1667
00:54:52,680 --> 00:54:54,080
Guess I'll have to summon a god.

1668
00:54:55,740 --> 00:54:56,820
(May the mighty Yu bless us)

1669
00:54:57,600 --> 00:54:58,440
Come forth.

1670
00:54:58,440 --> 00:55:00,100
Anyu!

1671
00:55:00,140 --> 00:55:02,460
(Here he comes)

1672
00:55:04,320 --> 00:55:05,080
I think it's Bai.

1673
00:55:05,080 --> 00:55:05,560
Really?

1674
00:55:06,280 --> 00:55:07,840
What did Bai say again?

1675
00:55:07,840 --> 00:55:09,280
