01:04:51,520 --> 01:04:52,720
That's way beyond making someone mad.

1951
01:04:52,880 --> 01:04:54,160
AI just wanted to anger him,

1952
01:04:54,160 --> 01:04:55,480
not destroy him.

1953
01:05:03,560 --> 01:05:04,400
It's Season 4 already.

1954
01:05:04,960 --> 01:05:07,040
Time we built up some bad blood.

1955
01:05:09,280 --> 01:05:11,220
(Still showing off that swan neck)
Everyone's always so nice.

1956
01:05:11,240 --> 01:05:12,520
We just keep getting closer.

1957
01:05:12,520 --> 01:05:13,600
What's wrong with you guys?

1958
01:05:15,100 --> 01:05:16,260
(You won't look like me
if you get too skinny)

1959
01:05:16,280 --> 01:05:17,360
My brain's stopped working.

1960
01:05:17,360 --> 01:05:17,920
Think. Quick.

1961
01:05:19,440 --> 01:05:21,000
Can everyone repeat their lines?

1962
01:05:21,200 --> 01:05:22,080
Except Bai.

1963
01:05:22,260 --> 01:05:24,460
(I'll never forget that insult)

1964
01:05:26,560 --> 01:05:28,160
You wanna hurt him all over again?

1965
01:05:28,920 --> 01:05:29,960
Bai's line was,

1966
01:05:29,960 --> 01:05:31,920
you should eat more.

1967
01:05:32,560 --> 01:05:33,720
Eat more.

1968
01:05:33,920 --> 01:05:35,200
She said you've lost weight.

1969
01:05:35,200 --> 01:05:36,320
And you won't look like him anymore.

1970
01:05:36,380 --> 01:05:38,820
(Already eating)

1971
01:05:41,080 --> 01:05:43,920
I really wanna pick Jingting.

1972
01:05:43,920 --> 01:05:45,440
If that was AI, fine.

1973
01:05:45,440 --> 01:05:47,040
But if he made that up, I swear...

1974
01:05:51,440 --> 01:05:53,040
How about Bai for our first guess?

1975
01:05:53,280 --> 01:05:55,120
Maybe it'll give him some closure.

1976
01:05:55,120 --> 01:05:56,640
Bai wouldn't really say that.

1977
01:05:57,320 --> 01:05:59,040
Did you make

1978
01:05:59,040 --> 01:05:59,920
the right choice?

1979
01:05:59,920 --> 01:06:03,060
(Praying for a miracle)

1980
01:06:03,480 --> 01:06:04,080
Congratulations.

1981
01:06:06,760 --> 01:06:07,040
Wrong.

1982
01:06:07,500 --> 01:06:10,620
(Bai Jingting: Wrong.
Flying off the scene)

1983
01:06:13,480 --> 01:06:14,040
Maybe the world

1984
01:06:14,040 --> 01:06:15,200
isn't so wonderful after all.

1985
01:06:16,420 --> 01:06:17,820
(Sorry, Chengcheng)

1986
01:06:21,160 --> 01:06:23,440
I was just looking out for Chengcheng.

1987
01:06:23,440 --> 01:06:24,680
(Big bro cares about you)
You're too skinny.

1988
01:06:24,700 --> 01:06:26,900
(Technically, he still loves me)

1989
01:06:27,560 --> 01:06:28,600
In northern Beijing,

1990
01:06:28,600 --> 01:06:29,960
(Instant relief)
Huairou's the prettiest.

1991
01:06:34,320 --> 01:06:36,260
(Still guessing)
Teng's reply seems suspicious.

1992
01:06:37,840 --> 01:06:39,920
He added so many filler words

1993
01:06:40,080 --> 01:06:42,000
to cover up his...

1994
01:06:42,480 --> 01:06:43,880
I told him to remove those.

1995
01:06:43,880 --> 01:06:45,120
All you'd have left is haha.

1996
01:06:47,800 --> 01:06:49,040
I think it's Teng.

1997
01:06:49,560 --> 01:06:50,240
Teng.

1998
01:06:50,240 --> 01:06:51,580
(Final choice: Shen Teng)

1999
01:06:53,080 --> 01:06:53,600
Correct.

2000
01:06:53,600 --> 01:06:54,020
(Shen Teng: Correct)

2001
01:06:54,020 --> 01:06:54,940
(AI reply: When we chat,
they always talk behind your back.)

2002
01:06:55,140 --> 01:06:56,180
(Second correct guess: +1 point)

2003
01:06:56,960 --> 01:06:57,680
Next scenario.

2004
01:06:57,780 --> 01:06:59,380
(Guessing team, Acting team)

2005
01:06:59,380 --> 01:07:00,320
(Scenario)

2006
01:07:00,320 --> 01:07:01,560
As a domineering CEO,

2007
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:04,560
you rush to his side with an umbrella.

2008
01:07:04,560 --> 01:07:05,800
What would you say

2009
01:07:05,800 --> 01:07:07,800
to make him
willingly give his all for you?

2010
01:07:08,680 --> 01:07:10,160
Come on, let's discuss it quietly.

2011
01:07:10,160 --> 01:07:11,960
(AI reply: Work hard,
but don't push your body too far.)

2012
01:07:11,960 --> 01:07:12,760
They're all the same.

2013
01:07:12,760 --> 01:07:13,400
Which is which?

2014
01:07:13,400 --> 01:07:15,000
Let's have one person say this.

2015
01:07:15,740 --> 01:07:17,580
(Forgot about that)

2016
01:07:19,440 --> 01:07:20,080
Turn around a bit.

2017
01:07:21,640 --> 01:07:22,440
Let's cover our ears as well.

2018
01:07:22,440 --> 01:07:23,720
So we can't even hear ourselves.

2019
01:07:24,920 --> 01:07:25,440
Secret meeting.

2020
01:07:25,500 --> 01:07:27,720
(Tuning out the world,
busy stuffing himself)

2021
01:07:27,720 --> 01:07:28,200
Could you...

2022
01:07:29,000 --> 01:07:30,880
maybe move away from the nut platter?

2023
01:07:31,880 --> 01:07:33,000
I'll stop after this handful.

2024
01:07:34,060 --> 01:07:35,620
(Just one more handful)

2025
01:07:35,920 --> 01:07:37,160
These aren't split open.

2026
01:07:37,160 --> 01:07:37,960
None of them are.

2027
01:07:38,480 --> 01:07:39,320
Hazelnuts have cracks.

2028
01:07:39,560 --> 01:07:40,720
These are chestnuts.

2029
01:07:40,720 --> 01:07:41,760
Just waiting for someone
to crack them open.

2030
01:07:41,760 --> 01:07:42,000
Right.

2031
01:07:42,400 --> 01:07:43,160
Just bite into them.

2032
01:07:43,160 --> 01:07:44,300
(Eating and burning calories
cancel each other out)

2033
01:07:44,480 --> 01:07:46,240
I think Bing should say this.

2034
01:07:46,240 --> 01:07:48,000
It sounds just like Bing.

2035
01:07:48,800 --> 01:07:50,240
It sounds like him.

2036
01:07:50,240 --> 01:07:51,760
It does.

2037
01:07:51,760 --> 01:07:53,440
(AI performance: Jia Bing)
Okay, sure.

2038
01:07:53,480 --> 01:07:54,520
You guys talk a little.

2039
01:07:54,520 --> 01:07:56,720
Stop nodding, bro.

2040
01:07:56,720 --> 01:07:57,560
It's too obvious.

2041
01:07:57,560 --> 01:07:58,040
Okay.

2042
01:07:58,480 --> 01:07:58,840
Okay.

2043
01:07:58,840 --> 01:07:59,200
We'll nod.

2044
01:07:59,720 --> 01:08:00,320
It's up to you.

2045
01:08:00,460 --> 01:08:02,700
(Acting before it even starts)

2046
01:08:02,700 --> 01:08:05,580
(AI performance: Jia Bing)

2047
01:08:05,600 --> 01:08:06,280
Just kidding.

2048
01:08:08,520 --> 01:08:09,320
I wasn't even watching you guys.

2049
01:08:09,320 --> 01:08:09,960
(No one cares)

2050
01:08:09,960 --> 01:08:11,360
Nobody's paying attention to you.

2051
01:08:11,640 --> 01:08:12,800
What are you hiding?

2052
01:08:13,100 --> 01:08:15,140
(A one-man show)

2053
01:08:15,640 --> 01:08:16,350
I'll go first.

2054
01:08:16,640 --> 01:08:17,430
I'll choose...

2055
01:08:17,960 --> 01:08:18,640
Jingyu.

2056
01:08:18,860 --> 01:08:19,760
(Scenario: Your employee heads home
on a rainy night)

2057
01:08:19,760 --> 01:08:20,780
(You're a domineering CEO)

2058
01:08:20,780 --> 01:08:21,970
(You rush over with an umbrella)

2059
01:08:21,970 --> 01:08:22,980
(What would you say to make them
give their all for you?)

2060
01:08:27,920 --> 01:08:28,600
Take out your phone.

2061
01:08:31,240 --> 01:08:32,390
Did you get your overtime pay?

2062
01:08:33,920 --> 01:08:35,040
Come in late tomorrow.

2063
01:08:35,040 --> 01:08:35,760
I don't want to see

2064
01:08:35,760 --> 01:08:37,390
any of my employees catch a cold.

2065
01:08:42,340 --> 01:08:43,500
(Coming back for dinner?)

2066
01:08:43,760 --> 01:08:44,840
Don't jump in the lake!

2067
01:08:44,840 --> 01:08:45,560
Come back!

2068
01:08:50,720 --> 01:08:52,700
(Like a horror movie)
I thought I was being robbed.

2069
01:08:55,120 --> 01:08:56,040
Take out your phone!

2070
01:08:58,640 --> 01:08:59,430
You scared me.

2071
01:09:00,250 --> 01:09:01,560
(Still shaken by Jingyu)
Not bad.

2072
01:09:01,840 --> 01:09:03,080
But that's definitely not AI.

2073
01:09:05,720 --> 01:09:06,240
Bro, come on.

2074
01:09:07,430 --> 01:09:08,640
When I reach the middle,

2075
01:09:08,640 --> 01:09:09,920
I want that umbrella in place.

2076
01:09:09,920 --> 01:09:10,430
(Don't let me get wet)
Okay.

2077
01:09:15,520 --> 01:09:16,390
No hood.

2078
01:09:17,040 --> 01:09:17,470
I'm already wet.

2079
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:19,040
I wanna go shirtless.

2080
01:09:19,760 --> 01:09:21,620
I don't want my clothes getting wet.

2081
01:09:21,620 --> 01:09:22,700
(Refuses to get rained on)

2082
01:09:28,390 --> 01:09:28,880
Bing.

2083
01:09:31,840 --> 01:09:32,160
Mr. Bing.

2084
01:09:33,470 --> 01:09:34,350
Work hard,

2085
01:09:37,080 --> 01:09:38,200
but don't overdo it.

2086
01:09:40,200 --> 01:09:40,640
Take it.

2087
01:09:43,270 --> 01:09:44,200
What about you?

2088
01:09:47,140 --> 01:09:48,580
(I'm free now)

2089
01:09:49,120 --> 01:09:50,840
Don't jump, Bing!

2090
01:09:51,640 --> 01:09:53,270
Now everyone's jumping in
the lake after acting.

2091
01:09:54,000 --> 01:09:54,400
Churan, your pick.

2092
01:09:56,560 --> 01:09:56,960
Hu.

2093
01:09:57,800 --> 01:09:58,240
Okay.

2094
01:09:58,240 --> 01:10:00,240
The two brain-fog buddies
are finally together.

2095
01:10:00,800 --> 01:10:01,720
Can't wait.

2096
01:10:01,720 --> 01:10:02,680
Mr. Fog and Ms. Fog.

2097
01:10:04,920 --> 01:10:05,720
You ran too fast.

2098
01:10:08,380 --> 01:10:09,900
(That's our Mr. and Ms. Fog)

2099
01:10:10,800 --> 01:10:12,360
Take your time getting out of the rain.

2100
01:10:12,840 --> 01:10:13,080
Come on.

2101
01:10:26,440 --> 01:10:27,040
Thanks.

2102
01:10:28,120 --> 01:10:28,720
My people...

2103
01:10:31,240 --> 01:10:32,640
wouldn't be left in the rain.

2104
01:10:36,000 --> 01:10:36,800
Whatever it is,

2105
01:10:38,000 --> 01:10:38,760
we'll talk tomorrow.

2106
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:39,440
Okay.

2107
01:10:46,080 --> 01:10:46,600
Lin.

2108
01:10:46,600 --> 01:10:47,160
Come on.

2109
01:10:49,280 --> 01:10:50,480
Lin, what's going on?

2110
01:10:51,240 --> 01:10:53,000
The first step to opening up.

2111
01:10:55,040 --> 01:10:56,800
I've been watching for ages.

2112
01:10:57,960 --> 01:10:58,360
Come on.

2113
01:10:59,040 --> 01:10:59,520
Well...

2114
01:11:01,960 --> 01:11:02,960
It's a right-hand-drive car.

2115
01:11:08,320 --> 01:11:09,600
What have I always taught you?

2116
01:11:10,360 --> 01:11:11,840
Didn't you bring an umbrella?

2117
01:11:14,600 --> 01:11:15,400
Take the car keys.

2118
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:17,520
Drive yourself home.

2119
01:11:25,000 --> 01:11:26,320
But I can't drive!

2120
01:11:29,640 --> 01:11:31,040
That's pretty extreme.

2121
01:11:31,560 --> 01:11:33,600
He didn't even offer him a ride.

2122
01:11:35,000 --> 01:11:36,280
That doesn't sound like AI to me either.

2123
01:11:37,120 --> 01:11:38,080
What did Churan say?

2124
01:11:38,560 --> 01:11:39,360
My people...

2125
01:11:40,280 --> 01:11:41,960
would never be left out in the rain.

2126
01:11:42,720 --> 01:11:44,640
Whatever it is, we'll talk tomorrow.

2127
01:11:45,120 --> 01:11:46,040
That's so Shandong of you.

2128
01:11:46,040 --> 01:11:47,540
(Questioned by a fellow Shandong native)
That's an inverted sentence.

2129
01:11:49,400 --> 01:11:50,120
Can't AI

2130
01:11:50,120 --> 01:11:51,480
be from Shandong as well?

2131
01:11:51,480 --> 01:11:52,780
(What if the AI is from Shandong?)
Well.

2132
01:11:52,800 --> 01:11:54,160
our Shandong AI?

2133
01:11:54,880 --> 01:11:55,560
My people...

2134
01:11:55,800 --> 01:11:56,400
My people...

2135
01:11:56,600 --> 01:11:58,200
Would never be left out in the rain.

2136
01:12:00,520 --> 01:12:01,160
No.

2137
01:12:01,160 --> 01:12:02,560
They'd never get rained on, my people.

2138
01:12:02,840 --> 01:12:03,480
That's inversion, right?

2139
01:12:03,920 --> 01:12:05,040
No, that's just gibberish.

2140
01:12:06,560 --> 01:12:08,520
But I think the missing subject

2141
01:12:08,520 --> 01:12:09,800
might actually be

2142
01:12:09,800 --> 01:12:11,120
something AI would do.

2143
01:12:11,120 --> 01:12:12,640
Look at the last question.

2144
01:12:12,640 --> 01:12:14,520
That reply was pretty unclear as well.

2145
01:12:14,520 --> 01:12:15,480
Something about not being able
to take it.

2146
01:12:16,760 --> 01:12:17,560
Couldn't take it.

2147
01:12:19,000 --> 01:12:20,200
Was that really AI's fault?

2148
01:12:20,380 --> 01:12:23,100
(Defending AI)

2149
01:12:24,160 --> 01:12:24,640
Village chief.

2150
01:12:25,000 --> 01:12:26,360
It's definitely AI's fault.

2151
01:12:27,000 --> 01:12:27,480
I'm right here.

2152
01:12:27,480 --> 01:12:28,480
I'll speak however I want.

2153
01:12:28,500 --> 01:12:29,800
(Confidence from being a local)

2154
01:12:29,800 --> 01:12:30,360
Nothing wrong with that.

2155
01:12:30,720 --> 01:12:31,520
Churan seems likely.

2156
01:12:32,400 --> 01:12:33,240
Churan seems likely.

2157
01:12:33,800 --> 01:12:34,320
Because

2158
01:12:34,320 --> 01:12:35,880
when they got the question cards,

2159
01:12:36,240 --> 01:12:38,040
Bing and the others
were at least thinking

2160
01:12:38,040 --> 01:12:39,520
about what to say.

2161
01:12:39,520 --> 01:12:40,360
But Churan was like this...

2162
01:12:53,320 --> 01:12:54,840
She went straight into

2163
01:12:55,240 --> 01:12:56,600
memorization mode.

2164
01:12:57,680 --> 01:12:59,880
She wasn't thinking about what to say.

2165
01:12:59,880 --> 01:13:00,320
She was just memorizing.

2166
01:13:01,300 --> 01:13:02,420
(Already in another dimension)

2167
01:13:06,280 --> 01:13:07,680
Bro, that impression was spot-on.

2168
01:13:22,520 --> 01:13:23,320
That's called...

2169
01:13:23,320 --> 01:13:24,160
flow state.

2170
01:13:24,920 --> 01:13:25,440
Churan, maybe?

2171
01:13:26,000 --> 01:13:26,960
You decide.

2172
01:13:26,960 --> 01:13:27,800
Oh my God.

2173
01:13:27,800 --> 01:13:28,880
After all that advice,

2174
01:13:28,880 --> 01:13:29,840
you decide.

2175
01:13:30,440 --> 01:13:31,200
Let the village chief decide!

2176
01:13:31,200 --> 01:13:32,960
(Passing the pressure)

2177
01:13:32,960 --> 01:13:33,870
Churan.

2178
01:13:34,020 --> 01:13:35,500
(Final choice: Wang Churan)
Churan.

2179
01:13:35,840 --> 01:13:36,880
Did the village chief

2180
01:13:36,880 --> 01:13:38,360
get it right this round?

2181
01:13:40,120 --> 01:13:40,560
Congrats.

2182
01:13:40,560 --> 01:13:41,280
You're wrong.

2183
01:13:41,460 --> 01:13:43,020
(Wang Churan: Incorrect)

2184
01:13:43,680 --> 01:13:45,360
This spot really brings me luck.

2185
01:13:47,880 --> 01:13:49,200
I told you it was Li Yunrui.

2186
01:13:49,200 --> 01:13:50,120
(Still guessing)

2187
01:13:50,120 --> 01:13:50,960
When did you say that?

2188
01:13:50,960 --> 01:13:52,040
Roll back the footage.

2189
01:13:52,360 --> 01:13:53,240
Let's watch the replay.

2190
01:13:53,260 --> 01:13:54,300
(Just kidding)

2191
01:13:54,360 --> 01:13:56,920
But after reading the question card,

2192
01:13:56,920 --> 01:13:58,600
Bing's reaction

2193
01:13:58,600 --> 01:14:00,280
showed he was thinking

2194
01:14:00,280 --> 01:14:01,120
about what to say.

2195
01:14:01,960 --> 01:14:03,240
You said someone else wasn't thinking.

2196
01:14:06,720 --> 01:14:08,360
I really don't know Churan well enough.

2197
01:14:09,600 --> 01:14:10,560
I never knew she could

2198
01:14:10,560 --> 01:14:11,800
think without blinking.

2199
01:14:11,980 --> 01:14:13,740
(New achievement:
Thinking without blinking)

2200
01:14:14,640 --> 01:14:16,200
Thinking without blinking.

2201
01:14:19,040 --> 01:14:20,040
When Churan thinks...

2202
01:14:23,920 --> 01:14:24,360
Right.

2203
01:14:27,720 --> 01:14:28,600
The way you think is terrifying.

2204
01:14:30,360 --> 01:14:31,720
Chengcheng doesn't seem likely either.

2205
01:14:31,720 --> 01:14:32,320
It must be Lin.

2206
01:14:34,080 --> 01:14:35,680
Driving a right-hand-drive car.

2207
01:14:37,360 --> 01:14:38,120
I added that myself.

2208
01:14:38,760 --> 01:14:39,400
You made that up?

2209
01:14:39,880 --> 01:14:40,560
Overseas domineering CEO.

2210
01:14:41,760 --> 01:14:42,640
Catching up with his employee.

2211
01:14:43,160 --> 01:14:44,040
Normally,

2212
01:14:44,040 --> 01:14:45,440
if I saw a colleague

2213
01:14:45,440 --> 01:14:47,080
or employee caught in the rain,

2214
01:14:47,680 --> 01:14:49,040
I'd give them a ride.

2215
01:14:49,600 --> 01:14:51,160
I'd charge 80 for a 20-yuan ride.

2216
01:14:51,220 --> 01:14:52,600
(Wait, you're charging him?)

2217
01:14:52,600 --> 01:14:53,720
Rip him off like that.

2218
01:14:53,720 --> 01:14:54,600
What a rip-off.

2219
01:14:58,760 --> 01:14:59,840
Back to work tomorrow.

2220
01:15:01,400 --> 01:15:02,680
No, don't catch a cold tomorrow.

2221
01:15:02,680 --> 01:15:03,800
Come in late tomorrow.

2222
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:05,280
You got soaked.

2223
01:15:05,280 --> 01:15:06,240
So what? Sleep in a little.

2224
01:15:06,680 --> 01:15:08,360
But his body clock is already set.

2225
01:15:09,480 --> 01:15:11,200
You can't just wake up later

2226
01:15:11,200 --> 01:15:12,320
because you want to.

2227
01:15:12,600 --> 01:15:13,120
